-- Coalition War Campaign vessels, printed 150-177: the CS ground vehicles and
-- aircraft of Rifts World Book 11. 16 vehicles, 192 M.D.C. locations, 59
-- weapon entries.
--
--   CS Mark VII "Slayer" APC, printed 150-152
--   Coalition Mark IX EPC, printed 152-153
--   CTX-50 "Line Backer" Heavy Assault Tank, printed 153-155
--   CTX-52 "Sky Sweeper" Anti-Aircraft Tank, printed 156-157
--   CTX-54 "Fire Storm" Mobile Fortress, printed 158-160
--   Death Bringer APC (AFC-151), printed 160-162
--   CS APC Sky Lifter (AFC-060), printed 162-164
--   CS Command Car (AFC-101), printed 164-165
--   CS "Scarab" Officer's Car (AFC-103), printed 165-166
--   CS Skull Patrol Car (AFC-105), printed 166-167
--   CS Scout Rocket Cycle (AFC-111), printed 167-169
--   CS Warbird Rocket Cycle (AFC-115), printed 169-170
--   CS Wind Jammer Sky Cycle (AFC-033), printed 171-172
--   Black Lightning Combat Helicopter (CH-10), printed 172-174
--   Demon Locust Combat Helicopter (CH-12), printed 174-176
--   SF-7 CS Talon Stealth VTOL Jet Fighter, printed 176-178 (its weapon
--     systems 1-5 run onto printed 178, the first page of the ISS section)
--
-- The section contents on printed 150 put the Command Car before the Scarab;
-- the book prints the Command Car first (164) and the Scarab second (165).
-- It also lists the CS Mark V APC with "see Rifts RPG": no stats here, no row.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local <this file>
--
-- The book has a TEXT LAYER; offset +1, so printed N is cache p(N+1) and
-- pymupdf doc[N]. The text layer carries the digit cipher (2D4xlO = 2D4x10)
-- on these pages, and cache p151 (printed 150) is welded, its two columns
-- interleaved. It was used only to find things.
--
-- PAGES READ OFF A 200 DPI RENDER: printed 150-178, every one. Every number
-- here comes from a render.
--
-- BOOK SLIPS, stored as printed and noted on the row:
--   printed 151  the Slayer's height is 28 feet "(5.5 m)" overall, the body
--                18 feet "(5.4 m)"; printed 150 gives its wheels 8 M.D.C.
--                each.
--   printed 153  the EPC's weapon list has two CR-2T laser turrets; its
--                M.D.C. list has one Center Laser Turret. Its dual blast is
--                "4D6" with no unit.
--   printed 153/154  the Line Backer's prose gives the rear thrusters 250
--                M.D.C. each; the M.D.C. list gives 300.
--   printed 155/157  the CR-8 medium-range launchers (Line Backer, Sky
--                Sweeper) take "medium-range" missiles, "but heavy missiles
--                are standard".
--   printed 156  the Sky Sweeper's prose says a four man crew and a pair of
--                mini-missile tubes; the stat block says five crew and four
--                tubes. Its class reads Infantry Hover Tank though it runs on
--                treads. Printed 157 puts its medium-range launchers "in the
--                rear"; the M.D.C. list puts them on the sides.
--   printed 158  the Fire Storm's 60 mph is "(96.5 m)"; printed 159 says
--                driving on the ground is not possible, though printed 158
--                has it hover three to ten feet above the ground. Its
--                Command Center main body carries a single asterisk (the
--                called-shot mark) where the other main bodies carry two.
--   printed 166  the Scarab skims water at 110 mph "(160 km/93.5 knots)"
--                and is 20 feet "(5.4 m)" long; its C-40BT double blast is
--                "4D6" with no unit. The prose gives it a pair of infrared
--                headlights and a pair of rear jets; the list has four and
--                three.
--   printed 166/167  the Skull Patrol Car's prose ceiling is 1200 feet (365
--                m), its speed block 1500 feet (457.2 m); cruising 50 to 80
--                mph is "(80.4 to 144 km)"; water 110 mph "(160 km)"; its
--                plasma turret does "6D6 per blast" with no unit; each CR-02
--                launcher "contains a total of eight" but the payload is 2,
--                one per launcher.
--   printed 169/170  the rocket cycles' lasers, pulse lasers and particle
--                beam print their dice with no unit.
--   printed 172  the Wind Jammer's smoke covers an 80 foot area "in front of
--                it" from a rear dispenser.
--   printed 174  the Black Lightning's cruise is 100-200 mph "(160 to 329
--                km)" (the Demon Locust repeats it on printed 175); its eight
--                tube launchers carry "48 total; 24 mini-missiles per
--                launcher".
--   printed 176  the Demon Locust's wing rail guns are "controlled by a
--                gunner" and fire at the pilot's rate.
--   printed 176/177  the Talon's VTOL makes it ideal for "horizontal
--                launching"; it is "manufactured by" Iron Heart, yet its one
--                Air Wing flies out of Chi-Town; Mach 1.5 is "(1005
--                mph/1608)" with no unit. Printed 178's four top launchers
--                are described as "a pair".
--
-- PRICES. Twelve machines print a CS Cost; the EPC prints a Black Market
-- Cost. The Fire Storm, Death Bringer, Sky Lifter and Talon are "top secret"
-- and print only an ESTIMATE; following the South America, Spirit West and
-- Underseas vessels, an estimate is not a price, so cost is NULL and the
-- printed estimate is in cost_note.
--
-- NUMBERED ENTRIES that are not weapons - hand to hand, sensor notes, special
-- bonuses, features of note - are in the description, including every pilot
-- bonus. Smoke dispensers are weapon rows, with no damage. Several listed
-- weapons have no M.D.C. location (the Line Backer's concealed mini-missiles,
-- the Wind Jammer's nose laser and smoke dispenser, the Demon Locust's nose
-- rail gun and medium-range launchers); nothing is invented for them.
--
-- DESCRIPTIONS ARE PARAPHRASES, never the book's prose.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles
  (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air,
   speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, cost, cost_note,
   description, source_book)
VALUES
  ('cs-mark-vii-slayer-apc', 'CS Mark VII "Slayer" APC', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Eight: pilot, co-pilot, communications officer, intelligence officer and four gunners', 'Any mix of troops; common loads: 50-60 foot soldiers in combat armor; 20 foot soldiers and 10 Terror Troopers or Maulers; 40 SAMAS or similar light power armor; 20 SAMAS and 10 Super SAMAS; 20 troops on Scout Rocket Cycles with 10 SAMAS or 6 Terror Troopers or Super SAMAS; 10-15 Glitter Boy Killers, Hellraisers or Hellfires', '80 mph (128.7 km) maximum', 'None', 'None', 'Height 28 feet (5.5 m) overall as printed (the body is 18 feet (5.4 m) and the weapon turret adds 10 feet (3 m)); width 15 feet (4.6 m); length 44 feet (13.4 m)', '42 tons unloaded', 500, 28000000, 'CS Cost: 28 million credits. Exclusive to the CS military; not available on the Black Market.', 'Model Type APC, an infantry assault and transport vehicle: a heavily armored, fast front-line APC on eight 12 foot (3.6 m) puncture-proof Triax tires, its reinforced Death''s Head front built for ramming vehicles, robots and structures. Airlock-style double doors (outer and inner) on both sides and the rear, plus concealed escape hatches in the crew compartment ceiling and the turret. The troop bay is 34 feet (10.3 m) long, about 400 square feet with a 17 foot (5.2 m) ceiling, for troops, power armor, robots, small vehicles or supplies. Destroying two wheels costs 20% of speed; three on one side 40% and -40% to piloting; four on one side 60%, same penalty. Losing the four sensor bubbles loses radar, targeting and their bonuses. Usually blue-black. Nuclear, average 20 years. Sensors: the basic robot vehicle features, plus voice or eight-digit keypad locking hatches, a homing beacon and long-range radio; field kit of portable long-range radio, short-range radar, medical kit, ten signal flares, ten C-29 Hellfire plasma rifles and CP-30 pistols with three E-clips each, and two weeks of food and water for ten. Hand to hand (ramming): half speed ram 1D6x10 M.D., full speed 2D4x10 M.D.; a ram against a human-sized target in body armor or light power armor does 1D4x10 M.D. and throws the victim 4D6 yards/meters (lose initiative and three melee attacks); running someone over does 1D6x10+20 M.D. The carried troops can be released to fight.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.150-152'),
  ('cs-mark-ix-epc', 'Coalition Mark IX EPC', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Three: pilot, co-pilot and gunner', 'Standard is 10 troops including the crew; a SAMAS takes two places', '110 mph (176 km) maximum on land', NULL, 'About 20 mph (32 km); not designed for major water travel', 'Height 10 feet 7 inches (3.16 m); width 7 feet (2.1 m); length 15 feet 8 inches (4.75 m)', '7.5 tons fully loaded', 220, 6000000, 'Black Market Cost: six million credits and up for a new, undamaged, fully powered EPC with its armaments; as low as one million rebuilt and without weapon systems. Limited availability; still being tested.', 'Exploratory Personnel Carrier by Julius Rosenstein, a tracked infantry and scientific transport: a less deadly cousin of the Mark V APC built for long-range reconnaissance and exploration, armored enough to hold out and call for help. Common with Rift Containment Study Group teams, field scientists and recon teams. About four feet (1.2 m) of storage for clothing, supplies, weapons, specimens and personal items, plus two C-14 assault rifles, four C-12 laser rifles, one C-27 plasma rifle, one rocket launcher and eight fragmentation grenades. Cheaper to build than the Mark V; scarce in Chi-Town (SAMAS) and Free Quebec (Glitter Boys), increasingly used by Iron Heart for exploring its territory. Nuclear, average 10 years.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.152-153'),
  ('ctx-50-line-backer-heavy-assault-tank', 'CTX-50 "Line Backer" Heavy Assault Tank', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Eight: pilot, co-pilot, communications officer, intelligence officer and four gunners; two additional passengers', NULL, 'Hovering 150 mph (240 km); tight turns and quick stops. Usually hovers 3-4 feet (0.9 to 1.2 m) up, as high as 10 feet (3 m), and jumps up to 60 feet (18.3 m) in length. The air-cooled hover jets run 24 hours before overheating and then need a two hour cooling period.', 'None', 'Hovers across water at 100 mph (160 km); submerges to 2000 feet (610 m) and travels about 25 mph (40 km/21 knots) underwater, but cannot open its bay doors underwater without flooding and sinking', 'Height 14 feet (4.2 m); width 15 feet (4.6 m); length 20 feet (6 m)', '40 tons unloaded', 790, 32000000, 'CS Cost: 32 million credits. Exclusive to the CS military; not available on the Black Market.', 'Model CTX-50, infantry hover tank: a compact, fast, heavily gunned front-line hover tank on a triple-tier hover system - three movable hover jets per side, an undercarriage hover system and three big rear jets for extra speed. Only one hatch shows, the gunner''s on top; the whole Death''s Head face lifts to reveal the reinforced crew compartment. Destroying the Death''s Head plating exposes that compartment. Two side hover jets lost cost 10% of speed and -5% on sharp turns; all six cost 25% and -20% to piloting on sharp turns or special maneuvers; all three rear jets halve speed. No cargo. Blue-black or camouflage. Nuclear, average 20 years. Sensors: the basic robot vehicle features; field kit of portable long-range radio, short-range radar, medical kit, ten signal flares, ten C-50 Dragonfire rifles and CP-30 pistols with four E-clips each, a light rail gun, CTT-M20 or CTT-P40 as the top turret gun, and three weeks of food and water for ten. Hand to hand (ramming): half speed ram 1D4x10 M.D., full speed 2D4x10 M.D.; a ram against a human-sized target in body armor or light power armor does 6D6 M.D. and throws the victim 4D6 yards/meters (lose initiative and three melee attacks); a deliberate ram takes two melee actions. Being run over only pins the victim under the jets (2D4x10 S.D.C.) until the tank passes.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.153-155'),
  ('ctx-52-sky-sweeper-anti-aircraft-tank', 'CTX-52 "Sky Sweeper" Anti-Aircraft Tank', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Five: pilot, co-pilot-gunner, two gunners, and a communications officer, field scientist or intelligence officer (the prose says a four man crew); one more passenger can squeeze in', NULL, '90 mph (144.8 km) on treads; the nuclear supply gives indefinite mileage without overheating', 'None', 'None; not amphibious, but can slosh through water up to its turret (about six feet/1.8 m)', 'Height 10 feet (3 m) overall: the lower body is 5 feet 6 inches (1.65 m) and the turret adds 4 feet 6 inches (1.35 m); width 11 feet (3.3 m); length 16 feet (4.87 m)', '21 tons unloaded', 400, 25000000, 'CS Cost: 25 million credits. Exclusive to the CS military; not available on the Black Market.', 'Model CTX-52, a light anti-aircraft tank on treads (the stat block class reads Infantry Hover Tank): small, fast, low-profile and easy to hide or carry - it fits inside the Death''s Head Transport, Death Bringer and Fire Storm - and simple enough that a child could drive it. The 360 degree turret holds the two long-range lasers and a medium laser mini-turret that also serves as a gunner''s nest for sniping or rail gunning. Its guided missiles can be fired from their forward launchers at targets in any direction, ground or air. Depleting the main body also exposes the reinforced crew compartment. One tread destroyed halves speed and gives -20% to piloting on sharp turns or special maneuvers; both immobilize it. It avoids ramming and seldom fights on the front line, serving as tactical support behind the lines and at outposts, or as a mobile anti-aircraft and anti-missile weapon that keeps moving. No cargo. Blue-black or camouflage. Nuclear, average 20 years. Sensors: the basic robot vehicle features plus enhanced radar and communications.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.156-157'),
  ('ctx-54-fire-storm-mobile-fortress', 'CTX-54 "Fire Storm" Mobile Fortress', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Command Center: 2-4 division commanders, 30 combat officers, 20 communications officers and 60 crew. Each of the two Death''s Head Transports: 17 (pilot, two co-pilots, two communication engineers, two technical officers and 10 crew), 34 in all', 'Typical force of 782 combat troops (894 with the crew): a squad (6) of Skull Smashers, a squad (6) of Spider-Skull Walkers, a squad (10) of Glitter Boy Killers, platoons (40 each) of Scout Spider-Skull Walkers, Hellraisers, Hellfires or CS Cyborg Strike Troopers, Terror Trooper Commandos or CS Juicers, and Scout Rocket Cycles and/or Warbirds or other small aircraft, two platoons of Special Forces (60 in Striker SAMAS, 20 in Terror Troopers or other power armor), and companies (160 each) of Light Assault SAMAS, Super SAMAS and infantry. Plus several dozen small vehicles; another company of man-sized troops can be squeezed in and a company or two of power armor can ride the hull', 'Driving on the ground: not possible (printed 159). The prose (printed 158) has it hover three to ten feet (0.3 to 3 m) above the ground at 60 mph (96.5 m, as printed) maximum, typically half that.', 'Rises to 300 feet (91.5 m) to fly over forests, towns and small cities. Separated, each Death''s Head Transport flies 180 mph (288 km) up to 1000 feet (305 m); the Command Center alone manages 30 mph (48 km) and 100 feet (30.5 m). It can hover for days, land, and fly when needed; take-off from the ground takes about 15 minutes, 3D4 minutes in an emergency.', NULL, 'Height 76 feet (23.2 m); width 104 feet (32.7 m); length 240 feet (73 m)', 'Approximately 1250 tons fully loaded', 5000, NULL, 'CS Cost: top secret, but estimated to be over a billion credits.', 'Model AFC-500 (headed CTX-54), air and ground super fortress and command center, nicknamed the Super Fortress and Fire Storm Command Center; inspired by art by Wayne Breaux. Effectively two Death''s Head Transports joined by a command tower: a mobile headquarters and flying command post with medical, communications, strategic operations and support capabilities and an armored troop complement, power armor and light robots being its main force. Living space beyond the officers and crew is cramped, so it lands at a chosen base site and anchors a temporary field base (a few days to a few years, typically 2D4 months) with half its troops camped around it and a field army of 5000 to 30,000 beyond; it is usually held back until the enemy is ready to fall or CS troops are in trouble. 12 in service, 12 in testing, six under construction; the goal is one per Field Army (four divisions, 23,000-30,000 troops). It splits into three parts: each transport carries a pair of concealed forehead lasers (1D4x10 M.D. per double blast, 2000 feet/610 m), and the Command Center keeps all the heavy weapons and the troops; they rarely separate except for tactical advantage or evacuation. Each section is destroyed when its own main body is depleted; the Command Center''s 5000 destroys the heart of the fortress - weapons, life support, communications, sensors, hover systems and the Command Deck - and the two transports can detach and flee. Hand to hand: none (see troops). Sensors: the most advanced the Coalition had around 105 P.A. Nuclear plant plus secondary systems, estimated 50 years.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.158-160'),
  ('afc-151-death-bringer-apc', 'Death Bringer APC', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Eight: pilot, co-pilot, communications officer, intelligence officer and four gunners', 'Any mix of troops; common loads: 60-80 foot soldiers (with or without jet packs); 40 foot soldiers and 20 Terror Troopers or Maulers; 60 SAMAS or similar light power armor; 30 SAMAS and 20 Super SAMAS; 20-30 troops on Scout Rocket Cycles with 6-10 SAMAS escorts; 25-30 Glitter Boy Killers, Hellraisers or Hellfires', 'Hovers as low as four feet (1.2 m); that close to the ground, 200 mph (320 km) maximum', '400 mph (643.6 km); maximum altitude 6000 feet (1828 m). The air-cooled hover jets run 24 hours before overheating; a half hour to an hour of cooling every 8-10 hours allows constant operation.', 'Hovers across water at 100 mph (160 km); submerges to 2000 feet (610 m) and travels about 25 mph (40 km/21 knots) underwater, but cannot open its bay doors underwater without flooding and sinking', 'Height 36 feet (11 m) overall (the body is 26 feet (7.9 m) and the cannon turret adds 10 feet (3 m)); width 35 feet (10.7 m); length 86 feet (26.2 m)', '123 tons unloaded', 900, NULL, 'CS Cost: top secret, but estimated to be 80-100 million credits. Exclusive to the CS military; not available on the Black Market.', 'Model AFC-151 Death Bringer Death''s Head Transport, an air armored troop carrier and assault vehicle: a heavily armored flying APC that often drops power armor, small robots and troops on small flyers without landing, slowing and opening its doors so they rocket out. Land troops, small bots and small vehicles leave by ramps from the five bay doors; the big side Death''s Heads, each crowned by a laser turret, are reinforced doors that slide up for larger power armor, bots and vehicles. Four big banks of jet thrusters on the sides and three small ones at the rear center; losing one hover jet bank costs 25% of speed. Losing the main sensor loses radar, targeting and their bonuses. The troop bay is 70 feet (21.3 m) long, 2100 square feet with a 20 foot (6 m) ceiling. Usually blue-black. Nuclear, average 20 years. Sensors: the standard robot sensors plus a thermo-imager (2000 feet/610 m), infrared and ultraviolet optics, a rotating mouth searchlight and four infrared-capable landing/search lights (300 feet/91.5 m; searchlight 1000 feet/305 m), and enhanced radar tracking 96 targets at 200 miles. Special bonuses: +1 to dodge at cruising speed, +2 to dodge above 300 mph; trained CS pilots get +10% to pilot it.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.160-162'),
  ('afc-060-sky-lifter-apc', 'CS APC Sky Lifter', 'rifts', 'vehicle', '20: pilot, co-pilot, two gunners, two communication engineers and 14 cargo crew (six of them in Mauler power armor for heavy lifting)', 'As many as 18 thirty foot (9 m) robot vehicles; or 40 Hellraisers, Hellfires or Glitter Boy Killers; or 12 Spider-Skull Walkers; or 40 Spider Scouts; or 12 ground APCs or tanks with their crews and troops; or about 80 Warbirds, Scout Rocket Cycles or similar small vehicles and pilots; or about one battalion (640 troops in full combat gear) plus a half dozen small to medium vehicles or a dozen Super SAMAS or Terror Troopers', 'Hovers as low as four feet (1.2 m)', '400 mph (643.6 km); maximum altitude 6000 feet (1828 m). The hover jets run 24 hours before overheating and then need two hours of cooling; pushing on risks burning out a saucer.', 'Hovers across water at 100 mph (160 km); submerges to one mile (1.6 km) and travels 35 mph (56 km/30 knots) underwater, but cannot open its bay doors underwater without flooding and sinking', 'Height 88 feet (26.8 m), 118 feet (35.9 m) with the 30 foot (9 m) tail; width 100 feet (30.5 m) body, 200 feet (61 m) with the wedge-like wings; length 240 feet (73 m)', 'Approximately 1900 tons', 2300, NULL, 'CS Cost: top secret, but estimated to be 200 million credits. A Death''s Head transport has never been available on the Black Market.', 'Model AFC-060 Sky Lifter Death''s Head Transport, an air armored troop carrier: a giant robot and vehicle transport with a huge cargo bay and minimal weapons (a concealed cannon and concealed missile launchers), usually traveling in a convoy or escorted by a squadron of Sky Cycles, Rocket Cycles or SAMAS. Four side bay doors 22 feet (6.7 m) tall by 18 feet (5.4 m) wide with sliding ramps; larger loads use the rear cargo door, 50 feet (15.2 m) tall by 40 feet (12.2 m) wide. Lift and speed come from three saucer-shaped propulsion units on the belly and two rear jets; losing one saucer costs 30% of speed. The sensor cluster is the front quarter of the concealed gun housing, and losing it loses radar, targeting and their bonuses. Usually blue-black. Nuclear, average 20 years. Sensors: the same as the other Death''s Head Transports.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.162-164'),
  ('afc-101-cs-command-car', 'CS Command Car', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot; tail gunner optional', 'Four passengers comfortably; a fifth can squeeze in beside the tail gunner', NULL, '200 mph (321.8 km); cruising 80 to 150 mph (128 and 240 km). VTOL, hovers stationary, retractable landing gear; hovers from two feet (0.6 m) to a maximum of about 500 feet (152 m). Flies 96 hours continuously without overheating.', 'Skims the surface at 100 mph (160 km/85 knots); not a submersible, and sinks like a rock if the hover jets are turned off', 'Height 4 feet (1.2 m); width 5 feet 6 inches (1.7 m); length 11 feet (3.3 m)', '2.1 tons', 180, 650000, 'CS Cost: 650,000 credits. The Black Market, Northern Gun and other makers sell knock-offs complete with a light rail gun for 850,000 credits, 450,000 rebuilt. Good availability.', 'Model AFC-101 military transport, the Flying Command Car, nicknamed "The Platform": a reliable, quiet open-top hover jeep for officers, field commanders and combat troops, also used by Commandos, Special Forces and commissioned field officers and for parades and troop inspections. A light semi-transparent cover (15 M.D.C.) is rarely used; drains and light M.D.C. materials keep the weather out. The light rail gun and its tail gunner''s seat are in the back, and the gun folds away when the canopy is up. Mega-damage glass windshield; the Death''s Head eyes are high-intensity searchlights and the three small circles on each side are infrared headlights for stealth night driving. A pair of rear jet thrusters add speed. Losing a bottom hover jet costs 10% of speed, a rear jet 20%. About three feet (0.9 m) of storage behind the seats. Nuclear, average 20 years. Sensors: long and short-range radio, infrared optics and short-range radar.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.164-165'),
  ('afc-103-scarab-officers-car', 'CS "Scarab" Officer''s Car', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Two: pilot and gunner', 'Four passengers comfortably; a fifth or sixth can be squeezed in, cramped', NULL, '220 mph (352 km); cruising 80 to 150 mph (128 and 240 km). VTOL, hovers stationary, retractable landing gear; hovers from two feet (0.6 m) to a maximum of about 1500 feet (457.2 m). Flies 48 hours continuously without overheating.', 'Skims the surface at 110 mph (160 km/93.5 knots) as printed; submersible, 50 mph (80.4 km/42.5 knots) underwater, maximum depth 300 feet (91.5 m)', 'Height 7 feet (2.1 m); width 5 feet 6 inches (1.7 m); length 20 feet (5.4 m) as printed', '2.4 tons', 240, 1600000, 'CS Cost: 1.6 million credits. The Black Market and Northern Gun sell knock-offs complete with weapon systems for 2.1 million credits, 1.3 million rebuilt. Fair availability.', 'Model AFC-103 military transport: a fully enclosed, aerodynamic flying hover car of mega-damage steel and glass for commanding officers, government officials and visiting dignitaries, and sometimes Special Forces, Commandos and the Rifts Containment Studies Group; a pilot and gunner usually come with it. Four laser ball turrets sit where a car''s wheels would be - the pilot works the front pair, the gunner the rear - and a concealed pair of mini-missile launchers extends to fire. The Death''s Head eyes are high-intensity searchlights with infrared headlights beneath for stealth night driving; rear jet thrusters add speed. Losing a bottom hover jet costs 10% of speed, a rear jet 20%. About three feet (0.9 m) of storage behind the seats. Nuclear, average 20 years. Sensors: long and short-range radio, infrared optics and short-range radar.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.165-166'),
  ('afc-105-skull-patrol-car', 'CS Skull Patrol Car', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Two: pilot and gunner', 'Two passengers comfortably; a third can be squeezed in, cramped', NULL, '150 mph (240 km); cruising 50 to 80 mph (80.4 to 144 km) as printed. VTOL, hovers stationary, retractable landing gear; hovers from two feet (0.6 m) to a maximum of about 1500 feet (457.2 m) (the prose says 1200 feet/365 m). Flies 96 hours continuously without overheating.', 'Skims the surface at 110 mph (160 km/93.5 knots) as printed; submersible, 40 mph (64.3 km/34 knots) underwater, maximum depth 300 feet (91.5 m)', 'Height 6 feet (1.8 m); width 6 feet (1.8 m); length 11 feet (3.3 m)', '1.9 tons', 200, 1400000, 'CS Cost: 1.4 million credits. The Black Market and Northern Gun sell knock-offs complete with weapon systems for 1.8 million credits, 1.1 million rebuilt. Good availability.', 'Model AFC-105 military transport, the Flying Patrol Car: a smaller, lighter, less aerodynamic and slower relative of the Scarab, fully enclosed, with a heavy plasma turret on the roof and a pair of single-shot mini-missile launchers underneath. Used by the military and the ISS - mostly by the Army for border patrol, convoy escort, military police work and transport - and sometimes by wilderness scouts, recon teams and the Rifts Containment Studies Group. The two back seats sit behind a transparent mega-damage partition for prisoners. Jet thrusters on the undercarriage and at the rear; losing a bottom hover jet costs 10% of speed, a rear jet 20%. About three feet (0.9 m) of storage behind the seats. Nuclear, average 20 years. Sensors: long and short-range radio, infrared optics and short-range radar.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.166-167'),
  ('afc-111-scout-rocket-cycle', 'CS Scout Rocket Cycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One', NULL, NULL, '440 mph (704 km); cruising 80 to 150 mph (128 and 240 km). VTOL, hovers stationary, retractable landing gear; hovers from one foot (0.3 m) to a maximum of about 2500 feet (762 m). Flies 12 hours continuously without overheating.', 'Skims the surface at 210 mph (336 km/178.5 knots); not submersible', 'Height 4 feet (1.2 m); width 4 feet (1.2 m); length 11 feet (3.3 m)', '1000 pounds (450 kg)', 150, 850000, 'CS Cost: 850,000 credits. The Black Market and Northern Gun sell cheap knock-offs at half the speed but with similar weapons for 500,000 credits; 600,000 for a rebuilt CS vehicle. Good availability for the knock-offs, poor for CS rebuilts.', 'Model AFC-111 aerial military combat vehicle, nicknamed the "Slingshot" and Rocket Scout: a fast, very maneuverable, well-armed one-man rocket bike hardly bigger than a motorcycle, favored by Special Forces, Commandos and RPA "Fly Boy" aces for reconnaissance, search and destroy, guerilla warfare, surgical strikes and infiltration; a squadron of 6-10 can take down a lone giant robot, tank or Glitter Boy. Four rapid-fire pulse lasers in the nose and a pair of mini-missile launchers; directional ball thrusters front, sides, rear and bottom for stability and VTOL, and two tail jet engines. The Death''s Head eyes are headlights. Losing three or more directional jets gives -15% to piloting; one rear jet halves speed with -30% to piloting; both send it crashing. Room only for an energy rifle and three E-clips. Nuclear, average 20 years. Sensors: long and short-range radio and short-range radar. Combat bonus: elite RPA SAMAS pilots and RPA Fly Boys get +2 on initiative and two extra attacks per melee round piloting it.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.167-169'),
  ('afc-115-warbird-rocket-cycle', 'CS Warbird Rocket Cycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One', NULL, NULL, '400 mph (643 km); cruising 80 to 150 mph (128 and 240 km). VTOL, hovers stationary, retractable landing gear; hovers from one foot (0.3 m; four feet/1.2 m is considered safe) to a maximum of about 6000 feet (1828 m). Flies 24 hours continuously without overheating.', 'Skims the surface at 200 mph (321 km/170 knots); not submersible', 'Height 4 feet (1.2 m), 7 feet (2.1 m) with the 3 foot (0.9 m) tail; width 10 feet (3 m); length 12 feet (3.6 m)', '1.2 tons', 220, 1300000, 'CS Cost: 1.3 million credits. The Black Market and Northern Gun sell cheap knock-offs at half the speed, with two nose rail guns, no particle beam and no fusion bombs, for 900,000 credits; one million for a rebuilt CS Warbird. Fair availability for the knock-offs, terrible for CS rebuilts.', 'Model AFC-115 aerial military combat vehicle, the Warbird: a cross between the Slingshot Scout Rocket Cycle and the Sky Cycle, about twice the Rocket Scout''s size and armed for dogfighting and heavy combat against flying power armor, aircraft and flying monsters, though it can hit ground troops too; a favorite of Special Forces, Commandos and RPA "Fly Boy" aces. A triple-barrel rail gun in the nose, lasers and a particle beam above it, mini-missiles on the sides and fusion bombs toward the rear. Concealed directional thrusters front, sides, rear and top, and two tail jet engines. Losing three or more directional jets gives -15% to piloting; one rear jet halves speed with -30% to piloting; both send it crashing. Room only for an energy rifle and three E-clips. Nuclear, average 20 years. Sensors: long and short-range radio and short-range radar. Combat bonus: elite RPA SAMAS pilots and RPA Fly Boys get +1 on initiative and one extra attack per melee round piloting it.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.169-170'),
  ('afc-033-wind-jammer-sky-cycle', 'CS Wind Jammer Sky Cycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One; a passenger possibly, dangerous and uncomfortable', NULL, 'Has wheels and rockets along the ground at 0-200 mph (321.8 km) maximum, reaching 100 mph (160 km) in three seconds', '620 mph (992 km, almost the speed of sound); cruising 80 to 150 mph (128 and 240 km). VTOL, hovers stationary, retractable landing gear; hovers from one foot (0.3 m; four feet/1.2 m is considered safe) to a maximum of about 6000 feet (1828 m). Flies 24 hours continuously without overheating.', 'Skims the surface at 200 mph (321 km/170 knots) but skips along it, -20% to piloting to keep control; not submersible', 'Height 10 feet (3 m); width 8 feet (2.4 m); length 16 feet (4.8 m)', '2.2 tons', 220, 1800000, 'CS Cost: 1.8 million credits. Exclusive to the CS; nobody has made a knock-off of the old or new style Coalition Sky Cycle.', 'Model AFC-033 air assault vehicle: the infantry combat version of the AFC-023 Coalition Sky Cycle (now handed to the ISS for patrolling cities and nearby towns), faster and deadlier, used for border patrol, fly-by reconnaissance, rescue and bombarding ground troops. A concealed short-range laser in the nose for dogfights; the main weapons sit in a weapon appendage that looks like a ramp or storage hatch and opens to fire a pair of gatling rail guns and a mini-missile launcher. The circular depressions are directional thrusters; five lower tail jets and a large central thruster modulate speed. Losing three or more directional jets gives -10% to piloting; a secondary rear jet costs 10% of speed; the main thruster halves speed with -30% to piloting; losing all the rear jets sends it crashing. Room for a change of clothes, a rifle, a handgun and personal items. Nuclear, average 20 years. The pilot works every weapon at his hand to hand rate. Hand to hand: none. Sensors: the standard robot sensors and communications, including radar. Special bonuses: +1 on initiative, +1 attack per melee round, +2 to dodge at cruising speed and +4 to dodge above 250 mph.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.171-172'),
  ('ch-10-black-lightning-combat-helicopter', 'Black Lightning Combat Helicopter', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Four: pilot, co-pilot/gunner, communications officer/gunner and another gunner', 'Four human-sized passengers or two power armor troops (a pair of SAMAS adds to its punch and surprise)', 'Not possible', 'Hovers stationary, VTOL; 300 mph (480 km) maximum, cruising and attack speeds usually 100 to 200 mph (160 to 329 km, as printed). Ceiling 20,000 feet (6096 m); combat height for air to ground attacks 3000 feet (910 m). Liquid fuel range about 500 miles (800 km). Hauling a slung load cuts maximum speed to 80 mph (128.7 km).', NULL, 'Height 15 feet (4.6 m); width 10 feet (3 m) body, wingspan 17 feet 2 inches (5.23 m); main rotors 50 feet (15.2 m) across; length 40 feet (12.2 m)', '8 tons fully loaded', 200, 750000, 'CS Cost: 750,000 credits. Ishpeming and Golden Age Armaments both offer a knock-off for one million credits, but fuel can be hard to get.', 'Model CH-10 helicopter gunship, a Coalition combat helicopter introduced by Iron Heart as an inexpensive multi-purpose attack aircraft - no nuclear or high-tech engine, just liquid fuel - and now its workhorse for low altitude recon, rescue, inserting and extracting ground and sea troops, combat, infantry support, cargo hauling and defense; also used by the fledgling navy (NAC) for search and rescue and combat support. Roughly a match for Sky and Rocket Cycles, and can haul up to 20 tons (giant robots included) slung beneath it. A squadron of four to eight can destroy tanks, APCs and small to medium air transports and fight power armor, helicopters, troops and giant bots, but loses to swarms of power armor, the faster Rocket Cycles and the Death''s Head Transports. Losing one rotor blade knocks it off course (the pilot loses initiative and three melee actions that round or the next), costs 20% of speed and -20% on later piloting rolls; losing two brings it down, and a piloting roll at -40% makes a crash landing that wrecks the helicopter but leaves those aboard unhurt with half damage. A crash does 4D6x10 M.D. to the helicopter and crew and 1D6x10 M.D. to a 50 foot (15.2 m) radius. Features: doppler radar that tracks storms and fixes position, a winch and hook for people or supplies up to 20 tons, and the standard aircraft sensors, radar and long and short-range communications.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.172-174'),
  ('ch-12-demon-locust-combat-helicopter', 'Demon Locust Combat Helicopter', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Four: pilot, co-pilot/gunner, communications technician and a secondary gunner', 'A full squad (10) of human-sized troops or five power armor soldiers', 'Not possible', 'Hovers stationary, VTOL; 250 mph (400 km) maximum, cruising and attack speeds usually 100 to 200 mph (160 to 329 km, as printed). Ceiling 20,000 feet (6096 m); combat height for air to ground attacks 3000 feet (910 m). Liquid fuel range about 700 miles (1120 km) on extra large tanks.', NULL, 'Height 20 feet (6 m); width 12 feet (3.6 m) body, wingspan 22 feet (6.7 m); main rotors 60 feet (18.3 m) across; length 65 feet (19.8 m)', '19 tons fully loaded', 250, 925000, 'CS Cost: 925,000 credits. Ishpeming and Golden Age Armaments both offer a knock-off for 1.3 million credits, but fuel can be hard to get.', 'Model CH-12 helicopter gunship and troop transport, a Coalition combat helicopter from Iron Heart: bigger, deadlier and slower than the Black Lightning, and just as cheap to run on liquid fuel, with a long-range laser cannon, rail guns and a missile battery. Used for low altitude recon, rescue, inserting and extracting ground and sea troops, combat, infantry support, light cargo and defense; room for ten passengers or equivalent cargo. Features: doppler radar that tracks storms and fixes position, a winch and hook for people or supplies up to 20 tons, and the standard aircraft sensors, radar and long and short-range communications.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.174-176'),
  ('sf-7-talon-stealth-vtol-jet-fighter', 'SF-7 CS Talon Stealth VTOL Jet Fighter', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One, with seats for two more crew, typically a bombardier and a communications officer', NULL, 'Only for conventional take-off and landing and for parking or storage', 'Mach 1.5 (1005 mph/1608, as printed) maximum; ceiling 60,000 feet (18,288 m). Minimum glide speed 60 mph (96 km), below which it may stall and crash unless in VTOL. Cruising 250 mph (400 km) to Mach One (675 mph/1080 km); attacks on ground targets at 250 mph to Mach 1.5, air targets at top speed. Nuclear, but the jets overheat after 18 hours of continual use; an hour''s rest every four to six hours lets it fly for months.', NULL, 'Height 18 feet (5.48 m) with landing pads out, 14 feet (4.3 m) airborne with gear retracted; wingspan 65 feet (19.8 m); length 30 feet (9 m)', '16 tons empty, 22 tons fully loaded', 350, NULL, 'CS Cost: top secret, but estimated to be 70-100 million credits. Only just unveiled; no knock-offs.', 'Model SF-7 stealth combat aircraft, a fighter jet: a pre-Rifts supersonic stealth fighter recently put into production by Iron Heart, experimental, and meant for use against Tolkeen and the Xiticix; one Air Wing of 30 jets exists, flying out of Chi-Town. VTOL lets it operate from super-city roof hangars, bunkers, small clearings, big ships'' decks and sturdy flat roofs (1-61% chance the roof caves in unless it is a large mega-damage structure or built for helicopters or giant robots) on any flat surface over 40 feet (12.2 m) across, but it is a jet: it hovers only in VTOL, to land or take off. Its low profile, shape and stealth systems slip it past enemy radar even at medium to high altitude. The reinforced pilot''s compartment ejects whole (pilot plus up to two), parachutes down and floats; a distress beacon starts four minutes after ejection and runs a week, and the radio (1-79% chance to survive) reaches 50 miles (80 km) for about a week. Under the seat: a small first-aid kit, a gallon of water, a survival knife and a flare gun with four flares. A self-destruct fires on the pilot''s command or five minutes after ejection or impact. No cargo beyond the two rear seats. Nuclear, 20 year life. Sensors: the standard robot sensors plus enhanced doppler radar tracking 96 targets at 200 miles. Special bonuses: +2 to dodge at cruising speed, +4 to dodge at or above Mach One.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.176-178');

